  "citation": "Chen J; Dafflon B; Wainwright H; Tran A P; Hubbard S (2021): CLM simulated data at three FLUXNET sites and three SNOTEL sites in the Colorado River Basin. Watershed Function SFA. Dataset. doi:10.15485/1804121",
  "dataset": {
    "@context": "http://schema.org/",
    "@type": "Dataset",
    "@id": "doi:10.15485/1804121",
    "name": "CLM simulated data at three FLUXNET sites and three SNOTEL sites in the Colorado River Basin",
    "description": [
      "This data package includes 6 csv files that include Community Land Model (CLM) simulations for three Fluxnet sites (i.e., US-NR1, US-GLE and US-VCM) and three SNOTEL sites (i.e., ER-BT, ER-SP and ER-PK) in the Upper Colorado River Basin area. Data inputs include meteorological forcing data (obtained from Fluxnet and SNOTEL databases) and CLM-simulated evapotranspiration (ET) data from 2005 to 2016. These datasets support the development of subseasonal regime approach based on statistics driven Hidden Markov Model to assess intra- and inter-annual variability of ET, which improves our understanding of climate change's impacts on water resources and ecosystem dynamics in the Colorado River Basin."
    ],
